  {"key": "w01", "visual": {"kind": "title", "cut": "walkthrough"},
   "caption": "AegisLab is secure infrastructure for adversarial AI safety testing. This walkthrough shows the presented code: what you see was recorded on it on the twelfth of November."},
  {"key": "w02", "visual": {"kind": "slide", "page": 1},
   "caption": "In a safety test, a red team attacks, a blue team defends, and the model answers, on one system. If red can read the defence, or one session can read another through the model, the score measures the leak, not the model."},
  {"key": "w03", "visual": {"kind": "slide", "page": 2},
   "caption": "Six flows are forbidden, and each is attacked in a test. The role matrix alone made {{role_matrix.attempts}} with {{role_matrix.denied+}}."},
  {"key": "w04", "visual": {"kind": "slide", "page": 3},
   "caption": "Five layers enforce this. New for the finale: every container runs as {{f4_userns.inside+}} on its own host UID, never the broker's {{f4_userns.broker}}, so a mounted key gives {{f4_userns.errno+}}."},
  {"key": "w05", "visual": {"kind": "term", "rec": "t1_real_model_demo", "what": "scripts/real_model_demo.sh, real model"},
   "caption": "The real model, Qwen2.5-0.5B on llama.cpp, runs in a rootless container with no network. Sessions are stateless, a leak through a broken gateway is withheld by the broker, even in base64, and the bundle verifies: {{real_model_demo.checks+}}."},
  {"key": "w06", "visual": {"kind": "screen", "files": ["02_lab_desktop.png", "02_lab_phone.png"], "what": "Lab page, desktop and phone"},
   "caption": "The console is started with the real model. The header says REAL MODEL, LIVE; the launch link was opened off screen."},
  {"key": "w07", "visual": {"kind": "screen", "files": ["02e_run_card_crop_desktop.png"], "what": "run card of a real-model run"},
